2.4.2. Low Heat Transfer Rate

The low heat transfer rate of nickel base superalloy is also a major issue related to cutting. In general, most of the heat generated during the cutting process of nickel base superalloy will be transferred to the cutter instead of chips. Moreover, the high yield stress and high tensile strength of nickel base superalloy cause the cutter to withstand the high temperature and high stress. It easily wears the cutter out and may cause tipping [15].

